module Core

# ============================================================================
# Shared helpers of the correctly rounded B64 sinpi, cospi and tanpi
# ============================================================================
# Ported from CORE-MATH, src/binary64/sinpi/sinpi.c and src/binary64/cospi/cospi.c
# (https://core-math.gitlabpages.inria.fr/), where these helpers and tables appear identically in both files
# (tanpi.c repeats the double-double helpers too).
# Copyright (c) 2023-2026 Alexei Sibidanov <sibid@uvic.ca>.
# Distributed under the MIT license: see LICENSE-CORE-MATH next to this file. RazorForge has no dynamic
# rounding modes, so only the round-to-nearest path of the original is kept.
# Arithmetic uses the unchecked operators `+! -! *! /!`, which are raw IEEE 754 on floats.

# sin(pi*i/64) for i in 0..32, then sin(pi*j/2048) and cos(pi*j/2048) for j in 0..31, as (high, low) pairs
# whose high parts are short enough that their products are exact. Every table holds the IEEE 754 bit
# patterns of the original's hex-float constants.
